From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:17:42 -0400
Subject: fix: issue 34's slider, the full-screen band, and two test races

GitHub issue 34: the sidebar width slider applies a drag when it is
released. Live, each tick moved the sidebar, and with it the settings page
and the slider under a pointer that had not moved, so the knob bounced.
Full screen on the Mac (toolbar T8): with the address row hidden with the
collapsed sidebar, macOS's full-screen title bar kept the row's height and
showed an empty grey band over the page. In full screen the row stays and
slides in with the pointer, as Chromium's toolbar does.
S-302: the chip test borrows the debug page action, which no feature hides.
S-291: the list test sets its window's size, waits for the scroll into view
and says which case it was if its premise fails.

Why: two bugs the owner and a user reported, and two flaky tests.
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
